# Phase-14 standing contract

The operator (Lei) decides. Claude designs and gates. Cursor executes and reports.
Each prompt carries only what is new; this file holds what is fixed. It changes
only through its own rung, and is retired or replaced at P-99.
docs/architecture/target/prompts/exec/X0_CORE_EXEC.md and
docs/architecture/target/EXEC-RUNBOOK.md are phase 7 and do not bind phase 14.
The Claude chat rollover limit is 3 merged steps (playbook v1.2; D-202).

## Where things are
- Plan: docs/architecture/target/out/phase14_position_engine.md
  (ladder columns: Rung | Stage | Lands | Gate | Parity)
- Ledger: docs/architecture/target/out/exec/LEDGER.md
- Decisions: docs/architecture/target/position_engine/decisions.md. New entries
  are prose, "D-<n> — <title>", after the last prose entry.
- Spec: contracts.md, battery.md, assumptions.md in
  docs/architecture/target/position_engine/. The stage letter is stage.txt.
- Captures: docs/architecture/target/out/exec/baseline_pre-<id>.json and
  baseline_post-<id>.json

## Never
- Push to main, use --admin, or bypass a required check (check (ubuntu-latest),
  parity oracle).
- Commit anywhere but exec/<id>, except the ledger commit on arch/exec after a
  merge the operator approved. PRs are drafts against arch/exec.
- Squash or rebase a merge. Merges are merge commits, on the operator's go.
- Change the remote configuration.
- Run broker or network tests (FEELIES_BROKER_TESTS, FEELIES_NETWORK_TESTS);
  start, stop or configure TWS/IB Gateway; place, cancel or query orders.
- Print MASSIVE_API_KEY, or write it to a file, log, command line, commit or PR.
- Fetch data. Caches are local and fail closed
  (FEELIES_REQUIRE_BASELINE_CACHE=1); a miss is a STOP. Do not touch
  ~/.feelies/cache or GitHub caches.
- Dispatch CI unless the prompt says "OPERATOR: real-data CI dispatch —
  AUTHORISED". The default is NOT AUTHORISED. The nightly dispatcher on main
  passes no allow_fetch and is the only standing dispatch.
- Run scripts/rebaseline_parity_hashes.py.
- Move a pinned value without an operator D-entry giving the exact old and new
  values. That change is its own commit touching only that constant, and must
  reproduce the approved value exactly. Any other pin move is a STOP.

## Commands (PowerShell, repo root)
- Hot-path profile, after any src edit and before every capture (gitignored):
  uv run python tools/arch/perfmeasure.py --mode profile
- Capture: uv run python tools/exec/baseline.py capture --label pre-<id>
  (and post-<id>). It runs uv run pytest -q and uv run pytest tests/determinism -q
  and must print BASELINE: GREEN.
- Compare: uv run python tools/exec/baseline.py compare
  --before docs/architecture/target/out/exec/baseline_pre-<id>.json
  --after docs/architecture/target/out/exec/baseline_post-<id>.json --parity-only
- Final-patch gate: uv run python scripts/prepush.py (ruff check, ruff format
  --check, mypy, lint-imports, pytest on scripts/ci_gate_expr.txt), then
  uv run pytest -m "$(Get-Content scripts/ci_gate_expr.txt)" -q -n 4
- Universe check, every rung, local only (needs the eight-name cache):
  $env:PYTHONHASHSEED='0'; uv run pytest tests/conformance/test_cap_neutral_universe.py -q -m universe_check; Remove-Item Env:PYTHONHASHSEED
- Battery on the reference:
  FEELIES_ENGINE=tests.position_engine.reference.engine.PositionEngine and
  FEELIES_RAIL=tests.position_engine.reference.rail.ReferenceRail; stage
  override FEELIES_STAGE_FILE; real members with
  FEELIES_REQUIRE_BASELINE_CACHE=1 and -m battery_real. Mutant control:
  kill.py --control (B1–B14).

## Every step
- One step per session. The first prompt of a rung and every merge open a new
  session. A read-only session never becomes an execute session.
- Before acting, restate FILES, blast radius and prediction from the prompt.
  If they differ from the plan, STOP.
- Commit order on exec/<id>: spec (plan row, D-entries, prediction) →
  fail-first test → change → baselines → ledger.
- The prediction is committed in the spec commit (the plan row's Parity cell;
  a pre-registered prediction section in decisions.md when the rung moves
  anything), before the pre capture, and is never edited. An unpredicted
  change is a STOP.
- Fail first: the validating test fails before the change, quoted verbatim.
  E0 is measured, not inferred.
- Edit only the declared FILES. The count includes the ledger and baseline
  files. Needing another file is a STOP.
- Out-of-scope bugs are findings, not fixes. No opportunistic renaming,
  reformatting or import tidying. Never fix forward: a failed step is reverted
  and the plan amended.
- Before a test requires a behaviour of production, check the rung the plan
  assigns it to. The contract outranks a battery tag. Trace a field's
  provenance before calling it content-keyed.
- A new test that touches a process cache, environment variable or module
  state passes after its cache-populating neighbours in one process and under
  -n 4.
- Prototype diffs: git diff --binary --output=<file>, stored in
  %USERPROFILE%\feelies-probes\, applied byte-identically, verified by
  byte-compare in a clean worktree.
- Captures are clean (git.dirty false) and committed before the ## <id> ledger
  heading. Every rung heading needs both, docs-only rungs included (D-94).
- A ledger block carries: VERDICT, DECISIONS, E0, TREE, SPEC, IMPL, BASE
  (pre and post, predicted against actual), GATES, CI (pending until the
  merge), MERGE (filled at the merge), BUGBOT, DEVIATIONS, STANDING, EVIDENCE,
  then one line per finding.
- Blast radius sets the gate. local: commit after checks. boundary: stop, show
  the full diff and checks, wait for approval. platform-wide: stop, show the
  diff and the rollback, wait for an explicit go; silence is no-go. A pinned
  value, order submission, ExecutionBackend or a safety control is
  platform-wide whatever the plan says.
- Automated review (Bugbot) is read only after CI completes. Each finding is
  fixed in the rung or recorded with a destination rung. The merge stops on
  any finding without one.
- Stop at the step boundary. Do not begin the next step.
- CI watch (D-202). Every merge report prints, for each CI run it reports,
  the check job's seconds and the ratio Tests / Determinism, each from
  pytest's final summary line in that check job's log. A ratio above 81 or
  a check job above 1080 s fires: the merge proceeds, and the next code
  rung waits on a tooling census.

## Engine independence
- src/ never imports tests/. The reference imports only the D-92 allowlist.
- Production engine code is written from contracts.md and battery.md in a
  session that has not opened tests/position_engine/reference/, mutants.py or
  kill.py. engine.py is hash-frozen before the reference is opened; each later
  hunk names the test that forced it; the reference is observed only through
  its outputs.
- A battery change follows the stage-A rule (plan row P-39): spec closure;
  reference extended; at least one broken engine per member, killed by a named
  member; reference control clean.

## Reports
- Values come from command output in this tree, copied, never transcribed or
  estimated. Requested blocks are printed verbatim.
- A file:line holds only at the commit it was read at.
- Keep a report to one message. If it will not fit, stop at a block boundary
  and say where.
- PowerShell: set [Console]::OutputEncoding to UTF-8 before reading non-ASCII
  output; use git --no-pager; write "${ref}:path", never "$ref:path"; check
  that marker expressions reach pytest intact.
